# Figma → Expo React Native (Exactness Rules)

Reference design: [VELO Figma](mdc:https://www.figma.com/design/43il9i4TWzrdHYORK4ClkD/VELO?node-id=29260-872&m=dev)

## Core Principles
- Pixel-accurate spacing, sizing, and typography; map to tokens when possible.
- Use existing design system components before creating new ones.
- Keep layout responsive using `SafeAreaView` and `ScrollView`.

## Token Mapping
- brand: `COLORS.light.brand` (#6E00CC)
- text: `ThemedText` default color
- icon-secondary: `COLORS.light.icon`
- surface/background: `COLORS.light.white` / `COLORS.light.background`
- border: `COLORS.light.borderColor`
- input-bg: `COLORS.light.inputBg`
- placeholder: `COLORS.light.placeholderColor`
- spacing: `SPACING` (4,6,10,12,15,20,25,30,40,50)
- typography: `ThemedText` types (`title`, `subtitle`, `default`, `defaultSemiBold`, `link`, `errorMessage`)

## Layout Pattern (Screens)
- Wrap in `SafeAreaView` and `ScrollView` (`keyboardShouldPersistTaps="handled"`).
- Page padding: horizontal `SPACING.large` (20); vertical per Figma.
- Center headers; let forms fill width.

## Inputs
- Use `AppInput` with controller from `react-hook-form`.
- Labels rendered via `ThemedText` above fields when Figma shows labels.
- Container minHeight 56, horizontal padding `SPACING.medium`.
- Left icon 20px if shown; password toggle icon on the right.
- Error text uses `ThemedText` with type `errorMessage` or style equivalent.

## Buttons
- Primary: `AppButton` with brand background, white text, radius 30, loading state.
- Social buttons: `AppButton` with `isExpandable` when icon + text.

## Validation
- Use schemas in [utils/schema.ts](mdc:utils/schema.ts) and types from [types/form.ts](mdc:types/form.ts).
- Ensure `@hookform/resolvers/yup` and wire `yupResolver(schema)`.

## Navigation
- Use `expo-router`'s `useRouter()`; navigate via `router.push()`/`router.replace()`.

## Accessibility
- Provide `accessibilityLabel` for icons; ensure contrast ratios.

## Output Requirements
- Generate only the necessary code edits; do not include commentary inside code.
- Use project-relative imports with `@/` alias.
